            <ArticleTitle>Liver dysfunction in Turner syndrome and its relationship to exogenous oestrogen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1141-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MEG.0b013e3283614b75</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Liver dysfunction is commonly seen in women with Turner syndrome and can manifest in a variety of pathologies. In this review, we discuss the spectrum of liver anomalies associated with this syndrome, and discuss some possible aetiological factors and relationships with exogenous oestrogen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
